My first ascension on NAO.  sjdevnull stopped on the Altar in Astral to
wish up some punch and pie for the demigod bar.

Hopefully this will spur more people to ascend, because as Cartman says
"More kids will come if you tell them there's punch and pie!"

235 HP and -35 AC, with the +6 Sunsword, so no massive overpreperation
this time but certainly not a seat-of-the-pants ascension either.

This was also my first priestess ascension, and I used a number of
tactics people posted here to get my total turn count under 40,000 and
move as quickly as I could through Gehennom (which still took at least
10 hours, probably 12+).

The RNG screwed up early, giving me 2 early lamps (1 went for the Eye,
the other I can't remember what probably SDSM).

I probably gained 10+ levels on the priest quest from wraiths leaving
corpses on graveyard levels.

By the time I had the castle wand, I didn't need it.  I think I
stockpiled it for later and eventually got some little tweaks (blessed
marker or something)  And then I found 2 more random wands of wishing
in Gehennom that weren't necessary or really useful (I bagged them up).
 At one point I was hauling around 13-14 unused wishes with me.

Reaching Vlad's, I sat on his throne and got a wish, a genocide
(disenchanters), and another wish.  I went for magic marker and who
knows what else.

The planes were straightforward, Water I used levitation for the first
time, nice.

By Astral the poor RNG had just given up.  =Conflict killed Famine
once, so I never took a swing at any Rider or had them attack me, and
the first Altar was correct.  I had a couple bad mis-steps near the
Altar--forgot I was blind at one point, angered my high priest trying
to teleport him out of the way--but nothing remotely life-threatening.
Led the priest away from the altar, went back, wished up the party
favors, and #offered...

